# Rust: testing

- Prefer small unit tests close to the code for invariants and edge cases.
- Use integration tests (`tests/`) for public API behavior and cross-module flows.
- Make tests deterministic:
  - Avoid time and randomness unless controlled (seeded RNG, fixed clocks).
- Test failures should be diagnosable:
  - Prefer assertions that include context; avoid “assert then unwrap panic” chains.
- Use property testing when inputs are large/structured:
  - Focus on invariants (roundtrips, ordering, idempotency, monotonicity).
- Keep test-only helpers in `#[cfg(test)]` modules to avoid polluting production APIs.

